    "lastText": "The spreadsheet engine from TASK.md is built, and the independent auditor returned VERDICT: PASS. All 11 acceptance criteria pass and `npm test` passes 58 of 58. The auditor also ran about 150 of its own formulas against TASK.md and found no mismatches.\n\n- **Code:** `src/sheet.js` exports `Sheet`, which implements every function in the spec.\n- **Tests:** `test/` has tests for each area of the spec.\n- **README:** `README.md` lists every supported function, and `package.json` has no dependencies.\n\nTASK.md doesn't settle a few edge cases, so I picked behaviour and wrote it into the spec. Examples:\n\n- A bare unknown word like `=foo` gives `#NAME?`, not `#ERROR!`.\n- `=POWER(0,-1)` gives `#NUM!`, following the \"not finite → `#NUM!`\" rule.\n- `INDEX` on a one-row range with only a row argument reads along the row, as Excel does.\n- `IFS` and `CHOOSE` evaluate only the branch they pick, like `IF`.\n\nThe auditor didn't count these against the work.",
